{
  "_note": "Reviewed semantic-rename rules for stillwater's src/ slices (PLAN §5, campaign run 2026-10-14). Two kinds: `global` maps a program-scope name (declared by one slice, referenced by others) to a semantic name and is applied in EVERY slice by tools/apply-names.mjs — the tool refuses a partial application, refuses a name that appears as an eligible identifier inside a wholeFile vendor/machinery region (vendors are never renamed), and refuses a target that already exists as a spelling in the readable. `files` maps per-slice scoped rules (a function's own scope; `name:*` widens to everything nested). Vendor identifiers stay minified by construction (vendor regions are index-only). The achieved per-file maps are recovered into rename-map.json by tools/recover-scoped-map.mjs and re-checked by tools/verify-rename.mjs, tools/check-chunk.mjs and tools/audit.js.",
